  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nThe persistent ridge of high pressure across the region will \nstill be intact early in the week. By mid week a series of mid to \nupper level disturbances move through the Northern Plains and \nMidwest, disturbing the ridge. The ridge will flatten and weaken \nWednesday into Thursday, but seems to hold up enough to keep the \nsfc low and associated cold front north of the region. This would \nkeep any rainfall chances out of the long term forecast. Will \ncontinue with the dry forecast through the week with a bump in \ncloud cover Tuesday night into Wednesday as a shortwave slides \nthrough. Otherwise, look for high temps to remain in the 70s \nthrough the week with the warmest days occurring on Thursday and \nFriday in the upper 70s. Overnight lows will generally be in the \nupper 40s with some locations reaching the lower 50s.",
